senses.gloss:
उप-√ 1. कृ P. Ā. -करोति, -कुरुते, to bring or put near to, furnish with, provide, Mn.; Vikr.; Ratnāv.;
to assist, help, favour, benefit, cause to succeed or prosper, R.; Mn.; Megh. &c.;
to foster, take care of;
to serve, do homage to (with acc.; only Ā. by, Pāṇ. i, 3, 32; but See MBh. i, 6408), ŚBr.; Rājat. &c.;
to undertake, begin, set about, R.;
to scold, insult, Vop. xxiii, 25;
 उप-स्कृ (स् inserted or perhaps original) Ā. -स्कुरुते, to add, supply, Pāṇ.; Vop.; Siddh.;
to furnish with;
to prepare, elaborate, arrange, get ready;
to adorn, decorate, ornament;
to deform, disfigure, derange, disorder, spoil;
to take care for, Pāṇ.; Bhaṭṭ., Kāś.;
to bring together, assemble.

उप-√ कॄ P. -किरति, to scatter or throw down, scatter upon;
to pour upon, besprinkle, bestrew, ŚBr.; KātyŚr.; MBh. &c.;
 उप-स्-कॄ (with स् inserted or perhaps original) P. -स्किरति, to cut up, split;
to hurt, Pāṇ.; Vop., Kāś.

उपा-√ 1. कृ P. Ā. -करोति, -कुरुते, (Ved. impf. 1. sg. -अकरम्, 3. sg. -अकर्) to drive or bring near or towards, fetch, RV.; TS. vii; ŚBr.; ĀśvGṛ.; MBh. iii;
to commit to, deliver, make over, give, bestow, grant (कामम्, a wish), MBh.; R.;
to procure for one's self, obtain, MBh. iii, 10278;
to bring or set about, make preparations (for a sacred ceremonial), undertake, begin, TS.; AitBr.; ŚBr. xiv; Lāṭy.; Mn. &c.;
to consecrate, Mn. v, 7; Yājñ. i, 171.

उप-√ 1. कृष् P. -कर्षति, to draw towards or near one's self, Suśr.; BhP.;
to draw with one's self, draw or drag away, R.;
to remove, give up, MBh.

उप-√ कॢप् Ā. -कल्पते, to be fit for, be ready at hand, become, ŚBr.; BhP.;
to serve as, lead to (with dat.), R. v, 25, 21;
to take the shape or form of, become, be, BhP.; Mn. :
Caus. P. -कल्पयति (inf. -कल्पयितवै॑, ŚBr. iv, 5, 2, 2) to prepare, make ready, equip;
to procure, bring near, fetch, ŚBr.; KātyŚr.; Lāṭy.; MBh. &c.;
to allot, assign, MBh.; R.; Yājñ.; Kathās.;
to put or set up, turn towards;
to arrange, BhP.; Pañcat.; Prab.;
to impart, communicate, BhP.;
to assume, suppose, Sāh.

उप-√ क्रम् P. -क्रामति (rarely -क्रमति) Ā. -क्रमते, to go near, approach, come to, RV. viii, 1, 4; 21, 2; 81, 7; MBh.; R.; Megh.;
to rush upon, attack (only P. by, Kāś. on Pāṇ. i, 3, 39 and 42), MBh. xiii;
to approach with any object, have recourse to, set about, undertake, begin (with acc. dat. or inf. only Ā. by, Pāṇ. i, 3, 39 & 42), Lāṭy.; MBh.; Ragh. &c.;
to treat, attend on (as a physician), MBh.; Suśr. &c.

उप-√ क्लिद् P. to become wet;
to rot, putrefy:
Caus. -क्लेदयति, to make wet, soak, Car.

उप-√ क्षिप् P. -क्षिपति, to throw at, hurl against, BhP.; Sāh.;
to beat, strike, ŚBr.;
to strike with words, insult, accuse, insinuate, R.;
to allude, hint at, Sāh.; Mṛcch.; Daś.;
to speak of, describe, define, Sāh.; Sarvad.;
to commence, set about (a work), Mall.
